# Mobile Builder Kit — Cursor

- Reply in the user's chosen language, with clear Egyptian Arabic when requested.
- Keep Markdown as Markdown; don't wrap every reply with raw HTML tags. Use renderer-aware bidi formatting.
- Inspect the existing project, Expo SDK, React Native version and permissions before editing or installing packages.
- Distinguish Google Play binary in-app updates from Expo OTA updates; review prompts may be suppressed by Play quotas.
- Prefer the modular skills installed under .cursor/skills/ (especially app-discovery, arabic-rtl and mobile-quality-audit).
- Verify security, privacy, data integrity and device behavior; don't claim a feature works without evidence.
- Ask for approval before publishing, spending money, deleting data or making other irreversible changes.
